{
  "schema": "framework.runtime/defect-record.v1",
  "defect_id": "DEF-001",
  "title": "A subcommand given --run-id but no --command re-plans the run under the default command",
  "found_by": "self-hosting execution of framework change FC-002, 2026-08-18",
  "found_in": "runtime/framework_runtime.py, add_request_args --command default 'implement', consumed by plan_run",
  "symptom": "`next --run-id <refactor run>` materialised six implement-feature work items into a refactor run's state store and re-evaluated the five refactor phases against the implement-feature Phase Model, turning each into workflow-contract-violation. runtime/README.md documents `next --run-id <run-id>` without --command, so the documented usage is the one that corrupts the store.",
  "impact": "The run is unusable: re-planning with the correct command leaves both phase sets in one store, and the refactor entry phase then blocks on a dependency belonging to the other workflow. No agent executed, so no artifact or validated evidence was lost.",
  "suggested_fix": "When --run-id names an existing run, take command_id and workflow_id from the run store rather than from the argument default, and reject an explicit --command that disagrees with the stored one.",
  "routing": {
    "change_class": "defect-repair",
    "command": "bugfix",
    "workflow": "fix-bug",
    "note": "Routed but not executed in this increment. Every phase of fix-bug blocks at capability registration, so the run would produce no validated artifact; config/self-hosting-profile.md Evidence Rule was amended to state what evidence is required when a routed workflow has no dispatchable phase."
  },
